      "writtenOn": "2014-04-24T16:04:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Commands above 0xdc are not available on ARM platforms, since the cros-ec kernel driver still uses SPIv2 communication protocol.\n\nSuggest defining a version 1 struct for EC_CMD_GPIO_GET which takes a sub-command.  That\u0027s what we\u0027ve done with the lightbar, battery vendor data, etc. so we don\u0027t need to use as many command handlers.\n\nparams {\n   uint8_t subcmd;\n   union {\n      struct {\n         char name[32];\n      } get_value_by_name;\n      struct {\n         uint8_t index;\n      } get_info;\n   }\n}\n\nresponse {\n   union {\n      struct {\n         uint8_t;\n      } get_value_by_name, get_count;\n      struct {\n         char name[32];\n         uint32_t flags;\n      } get_info;\n   }\n}\n\nenum subcmd {\n    EC_GPIO_GET_BY_NAME \u003d 0,\n    EC_GPIO_GET_COUNT \u003d 1,\n    EC_GPIO_GET_INFO \u003d 2,\n}",
      "parentUuid": "a5104b96_09036d2e",
      "revId": "dc2c7a3e05eae00b4959508c636f333ff509d5bf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
